        "date": "2026-11-19T05:33:22Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(2d): Slot Undercut for T-slot, keyseat, dovetail and lollipop cutters\n\nFour cutter kinds with a head wider than the neck (t_slot, keyseat,\ndovetail, lollipop) and one operation that cuts with them.\n\nThe generator (machining2d::undercut) cuts a straight or circular slot\nat one depth. It changes Z at one XY station only, outside the wall:\ndown, sideways in, the centre pass and the radial stepover passes,\nsideways out, up. The pass offset comes from the widest point of the\ncutter profile, not from the tip. An entry slot too narrow for the\nneck is refused by name.\n\nThe verifier has a new mode (Mode::Undercut) and law: a move that\nchanges Z while material is in or over the head is UndercutLift\n(blocking), and a neck or holder band with material above its bottom\nis a ShankHit. Both are read again against the stock that the earlier\noperations left. The solid law reads a dovetail as a frustum and a\nlollipop as a full ball, and gives the head top the allowance of the\ntip.\n\nThe field stock removes the true profile as the union of the head and\nthe neck solid (Stock::simulate_undercut, SdfTool::Dovetail). The\ncolumn engines cut nothing for an undercut: a column cannot hold air\nbelow material.\n\nApp: OpParams::SlotUndercut (tag 44), the project file mirror, the\nstamp digest, heights, the part solid law, the kept-parts law. The\ngeneric MCP tools create and edit the operation and its cutters. UI:\nthe tool kinds, the operation page, five original icons. The starter\ncatalog has one cutter of each kind.\n\nFixes #1444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
